# Git commit messages

When creating commits, write messages that are short, descriptive, and in English.

## Format

- One line, ~50 characters max (hard limit: 72)
- Imperative mood: "add", "fix", "update", "remove" — not "added" or "fixes"
- Focus on **why**, not a file list
- Prefer conventional commits when they fit: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`

## Examples

```
# ❌ BAD
Updated some files and fixed bugs in the patient form and also refactored stuff

# ❌ BAD
src/components/patients/patient-create-form.tsx: change validation

# ✅ GOOD
fix: require phone on patient create

# ✅ GOOD
feat: filter appointments by employee
```

## Rules

- Never commit unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not put secrets, `.env`, or credentials in commits
- Keep the subject line only; skip a long body unless the change needs a brief why
